 the mass of a neutron is also about 1 amu.\nStep 6:  Since the number of electrons in an atom is equal to the number of protons, the total mass of the electrons is equal to the total mass of the protons.\nStep 7:  Therefore, the mass of the nucleus (protons + neutrons) is greater than the mass of the electrons.\nStep 8:  As the mass of a proton and a neutron are equal, the part of the atom with the least mass is the electron.", "new_cot_probs": [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "cot_prob": [-0.9331613779067993], "cot_step_prob": [-0.9496752619743347]}}}
